6. Roadmap

Phase 0–2 Years — Foundation

Objective: Establish basic conditions.

· Infrastructure: Stable electrification of workshops, reliable internet connectivity, creation of 2–3 robotics training centers per country.
· Import and integrate: Acquisition of 10–20 entry-level Chinese cobots (3–5 kg payload), training of 20–50 technicians on ROS 2.
· Pilot deployment: 3–5 sites (agricultural cooperative, agri-food SME, maintenance workshop).
· Success indicator: 5 operational sites with measured ROI, 50 trained technicians.

Phase 2–5 Years — Local Capability

Objective: Reduce dependency and build local capacity.

· Local maintenance: Creation of 5–10 regional maintenance workshops. Capacity to replace wear parts, reprogram robots, adapt tools.
· RaaS at scale: Launch of 3–5 cooperative RaaS platforms, serving 100–200 SMEs and cooperatives.
· Local data: Generation of operational data for fine-tuning AI models.
· Success indicator: 80 percent of maintenance interventions performed locally, 200 active RaaS users.

Phase 5–10 Years — Local Manufacturing and Autonomous Ecosystem

Objective: Capture more value and build productive sovereignty.

· Local assembly: Partnerships with Chinese manufacturers for cobot and AMR assembly in special economic zones. Target local integration rate: 30–40 percent.
· Autonomous ecosystem: Closed loop robots → production → revenue → data → local AI → better robots. Open-weight models fine-tuned on local data become strategic assets.
· Success indicator: 10–20 percent of national robot stock assembled locally, capacity to design solutions adapted to local problems.

